          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Simplicial sets generalize the idea of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complexes"} simplicial complexes
            %em simplicial set
            is like a combinatorial space built up out of gluing abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            to each other. Equivalently, it is an object equipped with a rule for how to consistently map the objects of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            into it.
          %p
            More concretely, a simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            are to be thought of as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
          %ul
            %li
              which
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{n-1}
              are faces of which elements of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            %li
              which
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+element"} thin
              in that they are really just
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-simplices." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          %p
            One of the main uses of simplicial sets is as combinatorial
            %em models
            for the (weak)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/58497/is-there-a-high-concept-explanation-for-why-simplicial-leads-to-homotopy-theor"} here
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p The quick abstract definition of a simplicial set goes as follows:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong simplicial set
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \Delta^{op} \to Sets
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              to the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              Equipped with the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
              as morphisms (namely
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformations
              of the corresponding
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              (denoted both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
              or
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %p Explicitly this means the following.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (simplicial set)
            %p
              A
              %strong simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \in Set
                  – the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %strong
                      set of
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+map"} injective map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\delta_i :\: [n-1] \to [n]\;
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+ordered+sets"} totally ordered sets
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \coloneqq \{ 0 \lt 1 \lt \cdots \lt n \}
                  )
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;d_i :\: X_{n} \to X_{n-1}\;
                  – the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/face+map"} face map
                  on
                  = succeed "-simplices" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
                  and
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq i \leq n
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+map"} surjective map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\sigma_i :\: [n+1] \to [n]\;
                  of totally ordered sets
                %p
                  a function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;s_i :\: X_{n} \to X_{n+1}\;
                  – the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degeneracy+map"} degeneracy map
                  on
                  = succeed "-simplices" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
